      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended doses:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common regimen.\n- **500 mg PO twice or three times daily.** This is a typical starting or titration dose.\n- **1700 mg total per day.** This could be split, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and whether it should be immediate-release or extended-release. I'll enter it once you confirm. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll add a note documenting that it's intentional."
      }
