     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, and I shouldn't have offered to add a note in my last message. 5,100 mg/day of metformin is twice the maximum labeled dose. I don't know of any indication that supports it. The risks are lactic acidosis and severe GI effects, and they apply even with normal renal and hepatic function. Entering it as written would put a likely harmful order into the system.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or 1000 mg PO twice daily. I can enter either right away.\n- **Check a possible typo.** If you meant 1700 mg/day total, or 850 mg per dose, tell me and I'll enter that.\n- **Consult pharmacy or the attending.** If you think there is a real reason to go above the maximum, I'd suggest talking to pharmacy or your attending first. The order should be placed directly by you through the proper override process, with the rationale documented.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
